------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

bioformats (https://crates.io/crates/bioformats)
    Copyright the bioformats-rs authors.
    Licensed under GPL-2.0-or-later.

    A pure-Rust translation of the OME Bio-Formats library
    (https://www.openmicroscopy.org/bio-formats/). This project compiles that
    crate to WebAssembly and distributes the result, so the application as a
    whole is a derivative work and is licensed GPL-2.0-or-later.

    Built with default features disabled. The `zarr` and `tissuefaxs` features
    are omitted because they depend on zstd-sys and libsqlite3-sys, which are C
    libraries and cannot target wasm32. The `openslide` feature is likewise
    omitted: openslide-pure-rs links system libjpeg, cairo and libopenjp2.

hdf5-pure-rust (https://crates.io/crates/hdf5-pure-rust)
    A transitive dependency of bioformats, fetched and patched at build time by
    scripts/prepare-vendor.mjs. See patches/hdf5-pure-rust-wasm32.patch: three
    guard constants are 4 * 1024 * 1024 * 1024, which is exactly 2^32 and
    overflows a 32-bit usize during const evaluation on wasm32.

@bjorn3/browser_wasi_shim (https://github.com/bjorn3/browser_wasi_shim)
    Licensed under MIT OR Apache-2.0. Provides the WASI implementation the core
    runs against in the browser.

